# 6. FIX PRODUCT IMAGE UPLOAD AND REPLACEMENT

There is currently a problem in the Add New Product section.

When attempting to add or update a product image, the interface appears to show the current image without providing a functional replacement process.

Fix this properly.

### Required functionality

When adding a new product:

- Provide a clear image upload area.
- Allow users to select images from their devices.
- Display image previews before submission.
- Allow multiple product images where supported.
- Allow users to remove selected images.
- Display uploading progress.
- Show successful upload confirmation.
- Save uploaded images to the existing application storage system.
- Ensure uploaded images persist after refreshing the page.

When editing an existing product:

- Display the currently saved image.
- Include a clearly visible Replace Image button.
- Allow the seller to select a new image.
- Display a preview of the replacement.
- Allow the seller to remove an image if appropriate.
- Save the new image and update the existing product record.
- Ensure the new image replaces the old image in all relevant product displays.

Do not require users to delete an existing product before they can change its photograph.

Support common image formats such as JPG, JPEG, PNG and WebP.

Implement file-size validation, image optimisation, upload error handling and appropriate storage permissions.

For multiple product images, allow sellers to select a primary image and rearrange the remaining images where practical.

Make sure the same image update is reflected across:
- Marketplace cards.
- Product details.
- Search results.
- Featured listings.
- Vendor storefronts.
- Related product sections.

Do not use local-only image previews as a substitute for saving the actual image to persistent storage.

